Known answers for highctidh

There are no official CTIDH test vectors. The CTIDH authors' software
(high-ctidh 20210504 and 20210523 from ctidh.isogeny.org, and the TCHES
2021 artifact) has no known answers: its test*.exp files are test
transcripts, and its key generation reads the system RNG. No other
CTIDH implementation found publishes vectors independent of highctidh.

The ctidh*.kat files here are therefore self-generated. Each one holds,
for one field size, three private keys from fixed splitmix64 seeds, two
public keys, a shared secret and a blinded key. They were generated on
amd64 with single-size Go builds and cross-checked with:

  - the Go packages linked together (kat_test.go);
  - the C library driven through its byte helpers (../kat.c);
  - the Python binding (../tests/test_kat.py);
  - all three on amd64, 386, arm64, s390x, ppc64le and riscv64,
    natively or under qemu-user (misc/test-kat-matrix.sh).

checksums holds, per size, checksums over a deterministic key
generation and key agreement loop (checksum_test.go and
../tests/test_checksum.py). They are a regression and
cross-architecture consistency check; their correctness rests on the
known answers above.

Reference values for 512 and 1024 from CSIDH

highctidh's 512 and 1024 parameter sets use the same primes as CSIDH's
p512 and p1024, and the class group action depends only on p and the
exponent vector, so CSIDH's independent reference code is an external
check for them. csidh-reference-512.txt and csidh-reference-1024.txt
hold outputs of csidh-20210627 (Castryck, Lange, Martindale, Panny,
Renes), from https://yx7.cc/code/csidh/csidh-latest.tar.xz as linked
from csidh.isogeny.org, sha256
565d33a8fd28f99fa1d6f6189ae965834fb599e97a4aadde20106dc65fad380f,
built with its own sources for p512 and p1024. Only its outputs are
used here.

Each "pk e=... A=..." line is the action of the exponent vector e on
the base curve, and each "ss e=... f=... A=..." line the action of f
on the curve that e gives. A is CSIDH's curve coefficient converted to
highctidh's public key encoding: Montgomery form with R = 2^512 or
2^1024, as little-endian 64-bit limbs. All vectors but the last three
pk lines and the last two ss lines of each file lie within both CSIDH's
exponent bound (5 for p512, 2 for p1024) and CTIDH's batch bounds; those
last lines use the private keys of ctidh512.kat and ctidh1024.kat, which
exceed CSIDH's sampling bound but not its action, and reproduce their
pk_a, pk_b, ss_a_b and blind_f_a.

511 and 2048 use CTIDH-specific primes that CSIDH does not have; their
known answers remain self-generated and cross-checked as above.
